4.3 Tokenization

Explain tokenization as the process of breaking text into smaller units called tokens.

Word Tokenization

Example:

«""I love learning NLP.""»

Output:

["I", "love", "learning", "NLP"]

Sentence Tokenization

Example:

«""I love NLP. It is useful.""»

Output:

["I love NLP.", "It is useful."]

Subword Tokenization

Explain that modern NLP models often divide words into smaller subword pieces.

Give a simple example such as:

un + happiness

Mention that the exact subword pieces depend on the tokenizer.

